module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**the declared-type inhabitance wall decides on the KIND OF THE OFFENDING VALUE rather than on inhabitance, so it refuses a kernel literal at a declared type and admits a WRONG COPRODUCT ARM at the same position.** DESIGN section 4b puts `values inhabit declared types` in the ordinary compiler floor, so a breach is a below-baseline safety regression and not a rung on the ladder." as NonEmptyStr,

    "READ FROM THE RELATION, NOT INFERRED FROM ITS NAME. `v1.compiler.infer` `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch_bounded` short-circuits at its second guard: `if is_kernel_type(name: actual_name) == false || actual_name == \"Unit\" { false }`. A `false` there is `no mismatch`, so an actual value whose authored name is not a kernel type leaves the relation before any formal type is consulted. Every position that consults this relation inherits that exit." as NonEmptyStr,

    "WHY THIS IS NOT `one more declared-type position needs a member`, which is the natural reading and the wrong one. `test.claim.declared_type_kernel_inhabitance_witness_test` records that the census enumerated fourteen declared-type positions from the grammar -- every `parse_type_expr` call site in `v1.compiler.parse` -- and that seven admitted an `Int` where a coproduct was declared. Those seven were closed. But the guard above sits INSIDE the relation those positions now consult, so closing a position does nothing for a non-kernel wrong value: the record-literal field seam was ALREADY closed for kernels (that witness cites `KHold { subject: 5 }` refusing there) and still admits a wrong coproduct arm. The uncovered half is not a position, it is every position." as NonEmptyStr,

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN ONE (2026-08-25, `gentle-eagle-360`, controlled fixture): with `AlphaRefusal` and `BetaRefusal` distinct coproducts and `Wrapper = WrapsBeta { cause: BetaRefusal }`, a fn returning `WrapsBeta { cause: c }` for `c: AlphaRefusal` is ACCEPTED, while the same field given an `Int` is refused and given an undeclared constructor is refused. The two refusals are what make the acceptance a measurement rather than an absence of checking." as NonEmptyStr,

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN TWO (2026-09-10, gunbc#10952, found by review 63271): `data bmc_rotation_route_disposition: Disposition = SingleAuthority`, where `SingleAuthority` is an arm of `ConstructionMechanism` and `Disposition` declares only `Terminal` and `Scaffold`. It rode FOUR GREEN REQUIRED CHECKS. Two independent observations that it compiled rather than being skipped: a `gunbc run` over that closure resolved it and failed only on a wrong function name, and the pull request was green on all four required checks with the row present." as NonEmptyStr,

    "HARM, AND IT IS THE SECOND SPECIMEN THAT SHOWS THE SHAPE. The review that found it concluded `the module therefore does not compile, and with it the whole witness closure` -- reasonable, and false. So the defect does not merely admit a wrong value: it makes a reader who assumes the floor holds derive a WRONG CONSEQUENCE from a correct observation. The author had four green checks saying the row was fine and a reviewer saying the module was absent, and neither was true." as NonEmptyStr,

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: this is NOT the evidence-overreach family (a receipt supporting more than its instrument established) -- nothing here is a receipt, and the claim is not about coverage. It is NOT `check_subject_shape_cannot_represent_the_state_the_check_detects` -- the relation can represent the state perfectly; it declines to look. The tell is a wall whose guard names a property of the OFFENDING VALUE (`is_kernel_type`) where the property under test is a RELATION between the value and its declared type." as NonEmptyStr,

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor, which is not a rung. The class is decidable and the authority exists -- `lookup_type_by_name` and the declared-type env are already in hand at the guard that exits -- so this is DESIGN section 5's `wall after grounding` with the grounding already present. CEILING: structurally guaranteed; a wrong-typed literal is authorable in source, so impossibility is not available, but no `Accepted` program need contain one. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS A CAPABILITY: an inhabitance judgment that decides from the FORMAL type's declaration for an actual value of ANY kind -- kernel, coproduct arm, record literal, alias -- SUFFICIENT FOR removing `is_kernel_type` from the guard entirely rather than adding a second relation beside it. A second relation keyed on coproducts would be the fork this row exists to prevent." as NonEmptyStr,

    "NOT CLAIMED HERE: how many of the fourteen positions admit a wrong coproduct. The guard's placement implies all of them, and I did not measure them one at a time. A census across the fourteen positions with a non-kernel wrong value is the honest next measurement, and it is probably worth more than any single new witness member." as NonEmptyStr,
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
